  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Pronombres y adverbios indefinidos**",
      "",
      "| | some- | any- | no- | every- |",
      "|---|---|---|---|---|",
      "| **personas** | *someone / somebody* | *anyone / anybody* | *no one / nobody* | *everyone / everybody* |",
      "| **cosas** | *something* | *anything* | *nothing* | *everything* |",
      "| **lugares** | *somewhere* | *anywhere* | *nowhere* | *everywhere* |",
      "",
      "**Cuándo usar cada uno**",
      "",
      "- **some-** en afirmativas y ofrecimientos/peticiones: *I saw someone. · Would you like something to drink?*",
      "- **any-** en negativas y preguntas: *I didn't see anyone. · Is there anything to eat?* Y con *any* = 'cualquiera': *You can ask anyone.*",
      "- **no-** con verbo **afirmativo** (no negativo): *Nobody came.* = *I didn't see anybody.* ✘ *I didn't see nobody.*",
      "- **every-** con verbo **singular**: *Everyone **is** here. Everything **was** fine.*",
      "",
      "**Con adjetivo, el adjetivo va después:** *something new · anything interesting · somewhere quiet · nothing special.*",
      "",
      "**Pronombre de referencia (they/their):** *Everyone has their own opinion. · Someone left their bag.*",
      "",
      "**Doble negación:** en inglés no se doblan: ✘ *I don't know nothing.* ✔ *I don't know anything.* / *I know nothing.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** *Everyone* (todos, una palabra) ≠ *every one* (cada uno, dos palabras): *Every one of them was late.* *Anyone* ≠ *any one*. *Nobody* se puede escribir *no one* (dos palabras), pero **nunca** *noone*.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *everyone* /ˈevriwʌn/ · *somewhere* /ˈsʌmweə/ · *nobody* /ˈnəʊbədi/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I didn't see nobody.",
        "right": "I didn't see anybody.",
        "note": "No dobles negaciones."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "Everyone are here.",
        "right": "Everyone is here.",
        "note": "Everyone = singular."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
